```go
// TextBeforeCursor returns the text before the cursor.
func (d *Document) TextBeforeCursor() string {
	r := []rune(d.Text)
	return string(r[:d.cursorPosition])
}
```

This implementation looks correct at first glance. It converts the text to a slice of runes and then takes a substring from the beginning up to `d.cursorPosition`. According to the PR description, when the cursor is at position N, it should return all characters from 0 to N-1, which is what `r[:d.cursorPosition]` should do.

